<section class="mx-auto mt-12 w-full max-w-4xl section-shell prose-shell scroll-mt-24">
  <h2>Find Any Missing Angle With Confidence</h2>
  <p>The missing-angle calculation is the simplest operation in right-triangle geometry: subtract the known acute angle from 90 degrees. Behind that subtraction sits the triangle angle-sum rule, which reserves half of every triangle total for the right angle and leaves the other half to the complementary pair. Whether the known angle comes from a roof rafter, a ladder, a staircase stringer, or a drafting layout, the method never changes: confirm the right angle, subtract from 90, and verify that the two acute angles total 90 degrees. Keep this page bookmarked for the moments when an angle is already known and only its partner is missing.</p>
